# Experimental SEQ 3/4: keyboard note entry, linked drone pitches and
# unequal event timing. Screenshots are for emulator review.
notips
tap PLAY
tap SEQ
expect view 9
tap SEQ
expect view 10
tap SEQ
expect view 18
# Step 1 is the Home Pitch note. The timeline must fill the picture at N=1.
wait 250
shot seq-single.png
# Add step 2 and enter a note with the physical keyboard.
spin K3 1
spin K1 1
tapkey b5
wait 300
shot seq-two.png
# SEL+K1 moves the note along the current tuning.
press SEL
spin K1 2
release SEL
spin K2 1
tapkey w5
# Edit a third and fourth step using the keyboard.
spin K3 2
spin K1 1
tapkey b7
spin K1 1
tapkey w9
wait 250
shot seq-four.png
# With Pitch Lock off, phase translates drone II's path and note markers.
set 74 0
wait 250
shot seq-phase-0.png
turn K4 25 150
wait 250
shot seq-phase-25.png
# Return to two steps, then edit Node 2 and the overall loop endpoint.
spin K3 -2
tap SEQ
expect view 19
spin K1 5
spin K2 20
spin K3 30
spin K4 20
wait 250
shot seq-timing-two.png
# The new fifth page has four independent transition curves.
tap SEQ
expect view 20
wait 250
shot seq-shapes.png
# Add nodes back, demonstrate independent placements.
tap SEQ
expect view 9
tap SEQ
expect view 10
tap SEQ
expect view 18
spin K3 2
tap SEQ
expect view 19
spin K2 4
spin K3 -2
wait 250
shot seq-timing-four.png
# SEL+PLAY starts, pauses, then resumes the progression.
press SEL
tap PLAY
release SEL
wait 1400
shot seq-timing-running.png
press SEL
tap PLAY
release SEL
wait 1400
shot seq-timing-paused.png
press SEL
tap PLAY
release SEL
wait 1400
shot seq-timing-resumed.png
# Plain PLAY stops. SEL+HOME remains the existing random-start.
tap PLAY
tap HOME
expect view 0
